1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.400
CASE FILE No. 5hmC · TARGET: 5hmC · Aberrant 5hmC changes are often linked to cancer

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.400
PENCIL NOIR · THE 5hmC CASE

3
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.900
WHAT IS 5hmC? A chemical mark on DNA. Abnormal changes are often linked to cancer

4
00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.900
THE CHALLENGE: 5hmC must be measured quickly and precisely. Three carbon electrode materials, compared

5
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.800
Electrochemically exfoliate pencil graphite in one pot

6
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.000
Tree-like graphene (teG) · Low cost · Eco-friendly · Scalable

7
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.700
Same 5hmC-DNA: which material adsorbs more? (REFERENCE: pG and GO, each compared with teG | THIS WORK: tree-like graphene (teG))

8
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.900
REFERENCE: Less conductive than teG | THIS WORK: More conductive than pG and GO (Illustration · not real shapes, amounts or speed)

9
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.400
5hmC-DNA ADSORPTION: REFERENCE LOWER THAN teG | THIS WORK HIGHER THAN pG, GO

10
00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:20.400
Compared with pG and GO, teG conducts better and adsorbs more 5hmC-DNA (with lower surface roughness (not the same as its tree shape))

11
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:21.600
Conductivity: Reference materials (pG, GO) Lower than teG | This work (teG) Higher than pG and GO

12
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:22.400
Surface roughness: Reference materials (pG, GO) Higher than teG | This work (teG) Lower than pG and GO

13
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.200
5hmC-DNA adsorption: Reference materials (pG, GO) Less than on teG | This work (teG) More than on pG and GO

14
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.400
12.6 fM detection limit on a teG-modified gold electrode (for 5hmC-DNA · 1 fM = 10⁻¹⁵ M)

15
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.700
WHERE IT COULD GO: A separate portable wireless system · Label-free, real-time sensing (OCP) (Printed mulberry-paper electrode · Wireless potentiostat · Android app)

16
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.000
DNA from cancerous vs non-cancerous cells · Tells their 5hmC levels apart (A comparison using genomic DNA from the cells)

17
